WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:11.480
In the Clarity AD trial, 1,795 people had mild cognitive impairment or mild

2
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.400
dementia due to Alzheimer disease.

3
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.320
Amyloid was confirmed in all of them.

4
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.040
They were randomly given the antibody lecanemab or a placebo for 18 months.

5
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.200
Did the treated group get better?

6
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:29.560
They did not. Both groups got worse, and the question is by how much.

7
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:38.580
The outcome was a score called CDR-SB, the Clinical Dementia Rating, Sum of Boxes.

8
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.080
A clinician rates cognition and daily function.

9
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.500
The score runs from 0 to 18.

10
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.280
Higher means worse, so a rise on this scale is a worsening.

11
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:58.060
Adjusted mean changes at 18 months were +1.21 with lecanemab.

12
00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.760
With placebo they were +1.66.

13
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.360
Both are rises, so the treated group did not improve.

14
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:12.780
It worsened less. That gap is some of the strongest evidence that removing amyloid

15
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:17.460
changes the disease, and also evidence that the drug did not stop it.

16
00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:20.753
First, the absolute difference.

17
00:01:21.573 --> 00:01:24.573
It is a plain subtraction of two amounts of worsening.

18
00:01:25.493 --> 00:01:32.273
1.66 − 1.21 is 0.45 points less worsening.

19
00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:37.273
The paper reports a difference of −0.45 points.

20
00:01:38.093 --> 00:01:43.813
Its confidence interval runs from −0.67 to −0.23.

21
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:47.443
Second, relative slowing.

22
00:01:48.363 --> 00:01:50.543
Use the placebo change as the base.

23
00:01:51.403 --> 00:01:53.963
Think of the placebo bar as the whole decline.

24
00:01:54.963 --> 00:02:00.483
0.45 divided by 1.66 is 0.271.

25
00:02:01.363 --> 00:02:03.463
That is about 27%.

26
00:02:03.463 --> 00:02:09.863
Check it. 1.66 × 0.729 gives 1.21.

27
00:02:10.967 --> 00:02:13.887
So what does 27% mean?

28
00:02:14.707 --> 00:02:16.807
It compares two amounts of decline.

29
00:02:17.487 --> 00:02:20.247
It is not a 27% gain in memory.

30
00:02:20.727 --> 00:02:22.787
It is not a fraction of patients helped.

31
00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:25.047
It is not anyone's prognosis.

32
00:02:26.347 --> 00:02:31.487
Relative slowing is a share of the placebo decline, and the treated group still worsened.
